<td>A SercDog patrol sweeps the block; lie low or run</td>
</tr>
<tr data-source-range="983:984">
<td>13–20</td>
<td>You find a sealed crate the corps forgot to log</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h2 data-name="npc-stat-block">NPC stat block</h2>
<p>The narrative form a Dream Master reads aloud: <code>@npc-stat</code> with a <code>####</code> name, a <code>&gt;</code> flavor line, the stat lines, and <code>#####</code> sub-headings for traits and equipment. The flavor line is a ruled line (a rail in the block’s rule colour), not a box. The stat lines are picked by position: the first paragraph after the <code>&gt;</code> is the primary line, set as a chip (its first line 12pt bold, cream on the block’s colour), and a second line in it (or the next paragraph) is the secondary, a small-caps tag (10pt); no markup is needed, <code>2 HP — 1 Damage</code> over <code>Fodder — Medium</code> is the whole convention. A description belongs inside the quote, not between the quote and the stat lines.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="991:1011" class="language-markdown">@npc-stat

#### Patchhead

&gt; See a Patchhead comin' at you, you best move. Ain't no reasoning with 'em.

2 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Usually Small to Medium

##### Traits

**Bloodlust:** Patchheads add 1 to their Damage whenever they hit a creature that is missing Hit Points.

##### Equipment

Weighted chains, shivs, knuckle dusters; junk shields or crash helmets.

@end-npc-stat
</code></pre>
<p class="dg-result">Result</p>
<div class="dg-stage">
<div class="section dc-section-panel dc-npc-stat" data-name="patchhead" data-source-range="1016:1017"><h4 data-name="patchhead">Patchhead</h4>
<blockquote>
<p data-source-range="1020:1021">See a Patchhead comin’ at you, you best move. Ain’t no reasoning with 'em.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>2 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Usually Small to Medium</p>
<h5 data-name="traits">Traits</h5>
<p><strong>Bloodlust:</strong> Patchheads add 1 to their Damage whenever they hit a creature that is missing Hit Points.</p>
<h5 data-name="equipment">Equipment</h5>
<p>Weighted chains, shivs, knuckle dusters; junk shields or crash helmets.</p>
</div></div>
<p>A block with several <code>####</code> entries breaks between creatures and never inside one; the title bar stays with the first entry. A block with no <code>####</code>, or one, is one creature, and it stays on one page by itself; <code>--dc-npc-stat-break-inside: auto</code> lets one split.</p>
<p>To set the entries in columns, put them in <code>@columns 2</code> inside the block: the bar and an optional intro stay above, full width.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="1041:1076" class="language-markdown">@npc-stat

### Street Crews

Two crews that work the same block.

@columns 2

#### Patchhead

&gt; See a Patchhead comin' at you, you best move.

2 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Small to Medium

##### Traits

**Bloodlust:** Patchheads add 1 to their Damage whenever they hit a creature that is missing Hit Points.

#### Grease Monkey

&gt; Hold still, this'll only sting a lot.

3 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Medium

##### Traits

**Quick Fix:** A Grease Monkey patches an ally for 1 HP once per scene.

@end-columns

@end-npc-stat
</code></pre>
<p class="dg-result">Result</p>
<div class="dg-stage">
<div class="section dc-section-panel dc-npc-stat" data-name="street-crews" data-source-range="1081:1082"><h3 data-name="street-crews">Street Crews</h3>
<p>Two crews that work the same block.</p>
<div class="gp-columns gp-columns-2" data-columns="2" data-name="patchhead-2" data-source-range="1087:1088"><h4 data-name="patchhead-2">Patchhead</h4>
<blockquote>
<p data-source-range="1091:1092">See a Patchhead comin’ at you, you best move.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>2 HP — 1 Damage
Fodder — Small to Medium</p>
