<h5 data-name="traits-4">Traits</h5>
<p><strong>Climb, Jump, Invisible.</strong> Unless it moves, your eyes slide right past it.</p>
</div></div>
<h3 data-name="the-stat-strip">The stat strip</h3>
<p>A table with an <strong>HP</strong> column and a <strong>Damage</strong> column is a creature’s stat line, and it is set as a strip wherever it sits: no marker, no change to the table. A cell that holds only a number (<code>1</code>, <code>20</code>) is set large and centred. This is what to write for a creature inside a skill’s ability text, where a section marker such as <code>@npc-stat compact</code> would end the skill.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="1167:1172" class="language-markdown">| Name | HP | Damage | Traits |
|------|:--:|:------:|--------|
| Beacon Bug | 1 | 1 | Climb, Jump, Invisible |
</code></pre>
