<h2 data-name="npc-sidebar">NPC sidebar</h2>
<p>A contact card floated beside prose: a <code>.dc-human-callout</code> inside a raw <code>.dc-sidebar</code>. It has a blue ID header band reading <em>Contact</em>, an ink border, a hard shadow and a solid ink strip foot.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="1249:1255" class="language-markdown">&lt;div class=&quot;dc-sidebar&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dc-human-callout&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vance &quot;Static&quot; Oyelaran&lt;/strong&gt; — Fixer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two cybernetic eyes, owes everyone. &lt;strong&gt;Hook:&lt;/strong&gt; the chip is real; the access tunnel on it is bait.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p class="dg-result">Result</p>
<div class="dg-stage dg-on-paper">
<p>The Dreamers are low on credits and lower on luck when the noodle-stall door swings open. A figure slides into the booth across from them, drops a battered data chip on the table, and waits.</p>
<div class="dc-sidebar"><div class="dc-human-callout">
<p><strong>Vance "Static" Oyelaran</strong> — Fixer</p>
<p>Two cybernetic eyes, owes everyone. <strong>Hook:</strong> the chip is real; the access tunnel on it is bait.</p>
</div></div>
<p>Read the room before you read the chip. A fixer who makes it back out the door clean is a fixer who knew the drone was coming. Either way, the job’s already in motion the moment Static sat down.</p>
</div>
</div></div>"
