exports[`rendered output 07-specialty-system.md matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"<div class="chapter dg-guide" id="ch-specialty" data-ch="7" data-source-range="0:1"><div class="page dg-doc chapter-7" data-name="the-specialty-system" data-source-range="2:3"><p class="dg-kicker">Chapter 7</p>
<h1 data-name="the-specialty-system">The Specialty System</h1>
<p class="dg-lede">The richest family in the book. A specialty wrapper sets the shape and color; inside it, an intro panel, an art plate, a catalog card, learning paths, and skill cards all inherit that identity. Authors never set a variant on a card — the parent decides.</p>
<h2 data-name="specialty">Specialty</h2>
<p><code>@specialty .&lt;name&gt;</code> is the parent scope. It emits nothing visible itself; every component inside it reads its clip-path silhouettes and accent color. Ten families ship:</p>
<p><code>augmerc</code> · <code>proxy</code> · <code>streetwarden</code> · <code>gutterdruid</code> · <code>cybersurgeon</code> · <code>wirephreak</code> · <code>technosorcerer</code> · <code>etherlock</code> · <code>dualist</code> · <code>generalist</code></p>
<p>The silhouette says what kind of specialty it is, on the card, its tab, the path banner and the intro alike: tech ones are crisp stair-steps and square bites (Augmerc, Wirephreak, Cybersurgeon), magic ones are facets and lozenges (Etherlock, Dualist, Generalist, and the Proxy’s gate), the Technosorcerer is torn, the Gutterdruid wobbly, the Streetwarden a sign-plate octagon. The title band spans its frame exactly and every cut stays clear of the type.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="19:26" class="language-markdown">@specialty .augmerc

… intro, art, learning paths, skills …

@end-specialty
</code></pre>
<p>Opening a new <code>@specialty</code> closes the previous one, along with every path and skill inside it. <code>@end-specialty</code> does the same, and so does the next <code>@chapter</code>, <code>@page</code> or <code>@section</code>: a specialty cannot straddle a page, so put a page break inside one with <code>@page-break</code>. A specialty is written one of two ways, <code>@specialty augmerc</code> or <code>@specialty .augmerc</code>, and both give the same wrapper. A skill belongs inside a learning path inside a specialty; the Problems panel flags a skill sitting directly in the specialty. Tokens the wrapper sets for its children: <code>--spec-accent</code>, <code>--spec-mid</code>, <code>--spec-dark</code>, <code>--spec-band</code> and <code>--spec-on-band</code> (the title-band fill and its type), <code>--spec-chip-bg</code>, <code>--spec-chip-fg</code> and <code>--spec-chip-edge</code> (the tier pill), <code>--dc-skill-tab-shape</code>, <code>--dc-skill-body-shape</code>, <code>--dc-path-title-shape</code>, <code>--dc-path-shell-clip</code>, <code>--dc-specialty-intro-title-shape</code>, <code>--dc-specialty-intro-clip</code>.</p>
<h2 data-name="specialty-intro">Specialty intro</h2>
<p>The title-banded panel on a specialty’s first page: the <code>##</code> name, the pitch, and a <code>###</code> spec tweak. The band is the specialty’s own signal colour, so ten specialties read as ten colours and ten values at a glance, and each carries its own register: the tech specialties an LED rim and a rule of LED dots, the magic ones a faceted plane, Streetwarden a hazard-tape rule, and Technosorcerer and Gutterdruid a torn bottom edge with no rule.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="33:50" class="language-markdown">@specialty .augmerc

@specialty-intro

## Augmerc

An Augmerc is muscle for hire. Street thugs, corporate bodyguards, deniable enforcers — the difference is gear, grafts, and how much of them is still original.

### Spec Tweak: **Wired to Kill**

Augmerc learning paths assume combat-grade augmentations. Without the implants, the Augmerc spends 1 extra AP to activate a path's abilities.

@end-specialty-intro

@end-specialty
</code></pre>
<p class="dg-result">Result</p>
<div class="dg-stage">
<div class="dc-specialty augmerc" data-source-range="55:56"><div class="dc-specialty-intro" data-name="augmerc" data-source-range="57:58"><h2 data-name="augmerc">Augmerc</h2>
<p>An Augmerc is muscle for hire. Street thugs, corporate bodyguards, deniable enforcers — the difference is gear, grafts, and how much of them is still original.</p>
<h3 data-name="spec-tweak-wired-to-kill">Spec Tweak: <strong>Wired to Kill</strong></h3>
<p>Augmerc learning paths assume combat-grade augmentations. Without the implants, the Augmerc spends 1 extra AP to activate a path’s abilities.</p>
</div></div></div>
<p>Tokens: <code>--dc-specialty-intro-bg</code>, <code>--dc-specialty-intro-title-bg</code>, <code>--dc-specialty-intro-title-color</code>, and for the band’s register <code>--dc-band-rule</code>, <code>--dc-band-rule-h</code>, <code>--dc-band-tick</code>, <code>--dc-band-tick-style</code>, <code>--dc-band-tick-w</code>, <code>--dc-band-rule-skew</code>, <code>--dc-band-rule-bleed</code>, <code>--dc-band-facet</code>, <code>--dc-band-facet-width</code>, <code>--dc-band-facet-clip</code>, <code>--dc-band-rim</code>, <code>--dc-band-reg</code> (a second ink printed 2px off, tech bands).</p>
<h2 data-name="specialty-art">Specialty art</h2>
<p>A full-page art plate. It takes its own page and bleeds to the edge; in a book this follows the intro. The rendered plate is the next page. The placeholders here are local PNGs in <code>design-guide/img/</code>, one per specialty.</p>
<pre><code data-source-range="79:90" class="language-markdown">@specialty .augmerc

@specialty-art

![Augmerc](img/specialty-augmerc-wide.png)

@end-specialty-art

@end-specialty
</code></pre>
<div class="dc-specialty augmerc" data-source-range="91:92"><div class="dc-specialty-art" data-source-range="93:94"><p class="dc-img-wrapper"><img src="img/specialty-augmerc-wide.png" alt="Augmerc" data-gp-source-token="![Augmerc](img/specialty-augmerc-wide.png)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0" data-name="specialty-augmerc-wide"></p>
</div></div><h2 data-name="specialty-card">Specialty card</h2>
<p>The catalog card for a “choose your specialty” page: portrait, a <code>&gt;</code> tagline, and a short pitch, inside a <code>@card-grid</code>, with <code>@columns 2</code> laying the cards out two across. Each card sits in its own <code>@specialty</code> so it carries its own color, its silhouette and its own portrait cut. On a <a href="#ch-templates" data-gp-source-token="[\`@page specialty-catalog\`](#ch-templates)" data-gp-source-occurrence="0"><code>@page specialty-catalog</code></a> the ten cards become a two-page spread of tall poster cards (portrait on top, then name, tagline and pitch); anywhere else they are the dense card, a small thumbnail beside the text. The card’s layout is tokens: <code>--dc-specialty-card-display</code>, <code>-media-order</code>, <code>-media-float</code>, <code>-media-margin</code>, <code>-media-shape</code>, <code>-media-mat</code>, <code>-name-size</code> and <code>-index</code>, and the grid’s <code>--dc-card-grid-display</code>, <code>-item-display</code>, <code>-row</code> and <code>-gap</code>.</p>
<pre><code class="dg-split language-markdown" data-source-range="106:147">@card-grid

@columns 2

@specialty .augmerc

@specialty-card #card-augmerc

### Augmerc

![Augmerc](img/specialty-augmerc-card.png)

&gt; Cybernetic Commando

Heavily armed and wired for war, Augmercs are the blunt force of any squad.

@end-specialty-card

@end-specialty

@specialty .gutterdruid

@specialty-card #card-gutterdruid

### Gutterdruid

![Gutterdruid](img/specialty-gutterdruid-card.png)

&gt; Feral Shapeshifter

Gutterdruids rewrite their own flesh to match the wasteland around them.

@end-specialty-card

@end-specialty

@end-columns

@end-card-grid
</code></pre>
